<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Trapped Western Deep miners freed.</title>
<headline>Trapped Western Deep miners freed.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fifteen miners trapped underground by an earthquake at Western Deep Levels east mine have been rescued, managers Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Early indications are that the men are well. However, they will be taken to the Western Deep Levels hospital for a thorough medical examination,&quot; the firm said.</p>
<p>One mineworker was killed, and a further 17 injured in the accident have been admitted to hospital.</p>
<p>The accident was caused by a seismic event which occurred at 0720 GMT and measured 3.1 on the Richter scale.</p>
<p>Western Deep produced 7,830 kg of gold in the three months to end September.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
